<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Show that \(a\) and \(b\) do not define the same function.</para>
    <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <para>Rewriting \(a\) in standard form gives \(x^2−10x+21\), and \(b\) in standard form is \(x^2−4x−5\).</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example></section>
